<title>USA: Harsco adopts revised rights plan.</title>
<headline>Harsco adopts revised rights plan.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG, Penn. 1997-06-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Harsco Corp said Tuesday it adopted a new shareholder rights plan to &quot;protect shareholders against abusive and unfair takeover tactics.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said the plan, which replaces the 1987 rights plan, is designed &quot;to prevent an acquirer from gaining control of the company without paying a full and fair price to the shareholders.&quot;</p>
<p>Under the revised plan, each share of common stock will be entitled to one right with an exercise price of $150, the company said.</p>
</text>
